   110	distinct reduced points or one colength-two DVR subscheme; two physical
   111	defect points over one base value are not a third alternative.
   112	
   113	## 3. Discrepancy, minimalization, and the four rows
   114	
   115	For `Delta=K_Y-r^*K_X`, adjunction with arithmetic genus gives
   116	
   117	```text
   118	Delta.E_i=2p_a(E_i)-2-E_i^2 >=0
   119	```
   120	
   121	on every minimal exceptional component.  The connected negative-definite
   122	intersection matrix has entrywise negative inverse, so `Delta<=0`; a
   123	connected Gorenstein block has zero discrepancy exactly when it is Du Val.
   124	
   125	Contract vertical `(-1)`-curves to the relatively minimal rational
   126	genus-one surface `S`.  With compatible divisor representatives,
   127	
   128	```text
   129	D=h_*Delta<=0,             K_S=F+D.                       (3.1)
   130	```
   131	
   132	The tame canonical bundle formula is
   133	
   134	```text
   135	K_S ~ -F + sum_i(m_i-1)P_i,
   136	F_i=m_iP_i,                deg fundamental line=1.        (3.2)
   137	```
   138	
   139	Since `rho(S)=10`, a horizontal `(-1)`-curve exists.  Intersecting (3.2)
   140	with it shows that two multiple fibres are impossible.  With none, its degree
   141	is one and it is a section.  With one fibre of multiplicity `m`, every
   142	multisection degree is divisible by `m`; a general plane-line horizontal
   143	divisor has degree three.  Hence `m|3`, giving exactly (0.2).
   144	
   145	For every fibre component `Theta`, `D.Theta=0`.  The connected fibre
   146	intersection matrix has integral kernel generated by the primitive fibre
   147	cycle, so a nonzero local part is
   148	
   149	```text
   150	D_t=-b_tP_t,             b_t>0.                           (3.3)
   151	```
   152	
   153	Support equality is on the **base**:
   154	
   155	```text
   156	Supp_P1(D)=Supp(T).                                        (3.4)
   157	```
   158	
   159	Contraction can discard internal discrepancy components inside a supported
   160	fibre; (3.4) says it cannot erase the whole defect fibre.  The two global
   161	intersection equations are
   162	
   163	```text
   164	m=1: sum_t b_t=2;
   165	m=3: b_0+3 sum_(t!=t0)b_t=4.                             (3.5)
   166	```
   167	
   168	Combining (3.4)--(3.5) with the exact length-two base scheme yields precisely
   169	the table in Section 0.  In particular a defect entirely away from the triple
   170	fibre cannot sum to four, and no `b_t` is identified with local geometric
   171	genus or GR length.
   172	
   173	## 4. Picard bounds
   174	
   175	For each blowup in the inverse of `h`,
   176	
   177	```text
   178	D_new=pi^*D_old+E,
   179	coeff_E(D_new)=1+ord_p(D_old).                            (4.1)
   180	```
   181	
   182	Proper surjectivity ensures that every `Y_t->X_t` has a component mapping
   183	onto the one-dimensional plane fibre; that component is not
   184	`r`-exceptional and has discrepancy coefficient zero.  Starting from
   185	`D_t=-bP_t`, every inherited component has coefficient at most `-b`, so a
   186	zero carrier must be born in the blowup chain.
   187	
   188	The satellite-safe induction is: before the first zero, if `M_j` is the
   189	largest fibre coefficient after `j` blowups, then
   190	
   191	```text
   192	M_j<=-b+j.
   193	```
   194	
   195	At a centre on one or several negative components the new coefficient is at
   196	most `1+M_(j-1)`; intersection and infinitely-near centres cannot accelerate
   197	the birth of zero.  Thus at least `b` blowups are required over that fibre,
   198	and counts over distinct fibres add.  Since `rho(S)=10`, the four Picard
   199	bounds are exactly those displayed in Section 0 for the minimal resolution.
   200	
   201	## 5. Exact local Hodge level and invariant gate
   202	
   203	At every complex DVR, Liu--Lorenzini--Raynaud Theorem 3.1 identifies the
   204	resolved-torsor Hodge lattice with the minimal Jacobian/Neron differential
   205	lattice, including the locally insoluble triple fibre.  The 2018 corrigendum
   206	does not alter that theorem.  With compatible generators, if the local order
   207	of `s` is `k`, Fisher's differential weights give
   208	
   209	```text
   210	c4_plane=s^4 c4_min,
   211	c6_plane=s^6 c6_min,
   212	Disc_plane=s^12 Disc_min.                                (5.1)
   213	```
   214	
   215	Cremona--Fisher--Stoll Lemma 3.2 applies without a solubility hypothesis and
   216	shows that the CFS level of the given ternary cubic is **exactly** `k`.
   217	Therefore
   218	
   219	```text
   220	k=1: v(c4)>=4, v(c6)>=6, v(Disc)>=12,
   221	     and [v(c4)<8 or v(c6)<12];
   222	
   223	k=2: v(c4)>=8, v(c6)>=12, v(Disc)>=24,
   224	     and [v(c4)<12 or v(c6)<18].                         (5.2)
   225	```
   226	
   227	The discriminant lower bound follows from
   228	`c4^3-c6^2=1728 Disc` once the `c4,c6` bounds are imposed; it is a control,
   229	not a third generator.  The upper disjunction in (5.2) must be implemented as
   230	a finite principal-open cover, not as another equality.
   231	
   232	For `m=3`, all fibre multiplicities remain divisible by three under pullback.
   233	The plane fibre has total degree three, so it is necessarily `3L`.  After
   234	constant normalization and `t0=0`, the exact global coefficient family is
   235	
   236	```text
   237	F=x^3+tG1+t^2G2+t^3G3.                                  (5.3)
   238	```
   239	
   240	This is finite-dimensional, not a finite set of orbits.  Normality and
   241	generic smoothness are open conditions and must remain literal localizations.
   242	Saturation computes a closure and may reintroduce bad boundary points; every
   243	survivor must be checked on the declared open and actually minimized.
   244	
   245	## 6. Controls, scope, and interface composition
   246	
   247	The reviewed diagonal cubics separate discriminant order from total-space
   248	normality and fibre multiplicity.  The generalized-Hesse control has
   249	
   250	```text
   251	(v(c4),v(c6),v(Disc))=(4,6,24)
   252	```
   253	
   254	but exact level one, not two; its minimal Jacobian has discriminant order 12.
   255	Thus discriminant order 24 alone is never a level-two certificate.
   256	
   257	The theorem-interface composition finds one immediate exact client: the
   258	separately frozen first-jet packet
   259	`bd-a2-d3-triple-line-first-jet-invariant-gate-sol56-20260830.md` reduces the
   260	triple-line normal chart to two repeated-root first-jet forms.  That packet is
