Proof: We recall that K sh has residue field k. The idea of the proof is that if
Φ is not of the form listed, then we can use Lemma 5.7 to find a smooth k-point
on the reduction, and use the Henselian property to lift it to a K sh -point, thereby
obtaining a contradiction.
